# Playtest report: Snake build-1

**Build played:** producer release `build-1` (`snake-build-1.zip`): game-developer 7c1966c588b8fc955cb4ad523837f2818295b942, artist 67a4583812e38b740765f4920b0e1485b7903382, assignment at producer 4f258dc.
**How:** unzipped and opened `index.html` straight from disk (`file://…/index.html?seed=7`, so no server) in headless Chromium 1.64 (Playwright), 1366×768. All steering was done with real keyboard presses (`play.py`: a bot reads the board from `window.__snake` and presses arrow keys; manual timed presses for reverse, double turn and self-collision). Audio could not be heard (headless): I only know the sound assets loaded (`__snake.ready` true, no console errors). Full log: `evidence/build-1/play-log.txt`; recording: `evidence/build-1/full-session.webm`.

## Verdict: playable start to finish; I found no defect against R1–R9. Minor notes below.

| Req | Observed | Evidence |
|---|---|---|
| R1 | Opens and plays from `index.html` over `file://`, no server, no console errors, no failed requests. | play-log.txt (`console issues []`) |
| R2 | Visible 20×20 grid inside a wall ring; snake moves right on its own after start, ~5 cells in 0.5 s (120 ms step), steady. | 02-playing.png |
| R3 | Pressing the reverse (Left while moving right) was ignored, no death. Up then Left pressed back to back: both applied in order, no self-reversal. 12 mashed arrows: no crash. Arrow keys never scrolled (page height == viewport). | play-log.txt |
| R4 | Over two games the bot ate 3 then 10 food: length 3→6 and 3→13 (exactly +1 per food), HUD score 3 and 10, updated as it was eaten. New food appeared each time, never under the snake. | 04-after-eating.png, 06-long-snake.png |
| R5 | Idle run into the wall: game over "You ran into the wall." Coiling a 13-long snake (Down/Left/Up) into itself: "You ran into yourself." Both ended the game at once. | 03-gameover-wall.png, 07-gameover-self.png |
| R6 | Title on load: "SNAKE" logo, arrow-key and goal instructions, Start button, "or press Enter / Space". HUD hidden on title. | 01-title.png |
