Also worked: pause with P (head frozen, resumes), best score shown and "New best!" on game over.

## Things that confused or could annoy (not failures of R1–R9)
1. **Arrow key does not start the game** on the title screen (only Enter/Space/button). The title text says so, but the brief's example allows an arrow key too; a player's first instinct is often an arrow. Low severity.
2. **Losing window focus pauses the game** (blur → Paused). Sensible, but the paused overlay is the only cue; fine.
3. On the game-over and title screens the board behind the overlay is dimmed heavily, so the final snake position is hard to see ("how did I die?" is answered by the cause line instead). Cosmetic.
4. Quick double turns feel responsive (queue of up to 3 turns), but a 4th rapid press within one step is dropped silently; I never hit it in play.
5. Pace (120 ms) felt comfortable for the first games; there is no speed ramp (out of scope per brief).

## Not covered
- Sound quality/loudness (no audio output in this sandbox).
